source: crates/nb-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
notability folders — Organise the library: folders, subjects and dividers

Usage: notability folders <command>

Commands:
  create      Create a folder
  delete      Delete a folder (--recursive)
  edit        Edit title, colour, emoji, lock
  list        List folders (--parent, --tree)
  move        Re-parent a folder
  order       Children of a folder in display order
  organizers  Legacy subjects and dividers
  rename      Rename a folder
  reorder     Change position among siblings

Global Options:
  --filter-output <keys>              Filter output by key paths (e.g. foo,bar.baz,a[0,3])
  --format <toon|json|yaml|md|jsonl>  Output format
  --full-output                       Show full output envelope
  --help                              Show help
  --llms, --llms-full                 Print LLM-readable manifest
  --schema                            Show JSON Schema for command
  --token-count                       Print token count of output (instead of output)
  --token-limit <n>                   Limit output to n tokens
  --token-offset <n>                  Skip first n tokens of output
